# Generated evidence exports
backend/tmp/
exports/

.vercel

# Appended by `vercel link`. `.env*` is broader than the block at the top of this file and
# sits after it, so it silently re-ignored `.env.example` — gitignore takes the last match,
# not the most specific. The negation is repeated here so the committed template survives
# no matter which rule matched it. Root `.env.example` only stayed visible because it was
# already tracked; a new one would have been invisible.
.env*
!.env.example

# Android release signing. The keystore IS the app's identity: lose it and no future build
# can update an installed app, leak it and anyone can publish one that looks like yours.
# Neither it nor the passwords belong in the repository.
*.jks
*.keystore
!apps/mobile/android/app/debug.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties
